      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "ece0f1b21f",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h6>Markdown in, deck out</h6><h1>dex</h1></header><div class="s-body"><p>Write a talk as one Markdown file and present it from the browser. This deck is its own manual: press m on any slide to see the Markdown behind it.</p></div></div>",
      "id": "dex",
      "index": 0,
      "layout": "title",
      "line": 7,
      "notes": "<p>The title slide. An eyebrow line (six #), one # heading, and a short paragraph make a title slide with no layout syntax. Press m to see this slide's Markdown, and m again to close it.</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "dex",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "data-len": "s",
      },
      "hash": "991c76dd63",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><div class="s-body"><p>Write the words. The layout follows.</p></div></div>",
      "id": "write-the-words-the-layout-follows",
      "index": 1,
      "layout": "statement",
      "line": 17,
      "notes": "<p>A statement. One short paragraph and no heading is set in very large type. Nothing on this slide says "statement"; dex reads it from what the slide contains.</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "Write the words. The layout follows.",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "data-section": "01",
      },
      "hash": "50f9ad381f",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h1>How slides work</h1></header></div>",
      "id": "how-slides-work",
      "index": 2,
      "layout": "section",
      "line": 23,
      "notes": "<p>A section divider. A # heading on its own, anywhere after the first slide, becomes a numbered section.</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "How slides work",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "634e8ca3de",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h2>Lists that build</h2></header><div class="s-body"><ul>
<li data-step="1">Write a list with plus signs and it appears one item at a time</li>
<li data-step="2">Press → or Space to show the next item</li>
<li data-step="3">Lists written with - or * appear all at once</li>
</ul></div></div>",
      "id": "lists-that-build",
      "index": 3,
      "layout": "default",
      "line": 29,
      "notes": "<p>Builds. Each plus item is one step. Press ← to step back. Builds can be turned off for the whole deck in the settings (press s).</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 3,
      "title": "Lists that build",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "e2f93455ba",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h2>What happens when you save</h2></header><div class="s-body"><ol>
<li>The file is split into slides at every line of three dashes</li>
<li>Comments are read
<ul>
<li>a comment of key and value pairs sets options for its slide</li>
<li>any other comment becomes a speaker note</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>The layout is chosen from what is left on the slide</li>
<li>The open deck updates in place, without losing your place</li>
</ol></div></div>",
      "id": "what-happens-when-you-save",
      "index": 4,
      "layout": "default",
      "line": 39,
      "notes": "<p>A numbered list with a nested list. Nested items appear with their parent. This note is a speaker note, shown only in the presenter window (press p).</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "What happens when you save",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "data-count": "3",
      },
      "hash": "909f636eb5",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h2>Two themes and a switch</h2></header><div class="s-cols"><section class="s-col"><h3>Paper</h3><p>A pale mint page with near-black ink, for rooms with the lights on. Press t to switch.</p></section><section class="s-col"><h3>Ink</h3><p>The same palette turned around, for dark rooms. Put <code>theme: ink</code> in the frontmatter to start there.</p></section><section class="s-col"><h3>Invert</h3><p>A comment of <code>invert: true</code> on a slide shows that one slide in the other theme.</p></section></div></div>",
      "id": "two-themes-and-a-switch",
