    {
      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "bc4a81a2c0",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h2>Sources go in footnotes</h2></header><div class="s-body"><p>Every slide is laid out on a fixed canvas of 1600 by 900 points and scaled to fit the screen.<sup><a href="#fn-bc4a81a2c0-fn-stage" id="fn-bc4a81a2c0-fnref-stage" data-footnote-ref="" aria-describedby="footnote-label">1</a></sup></p></div></div>
<section data-footnotes="" class="footnotes"><h2 class="sr-only" id="footnote-label">Footnotes</h2>
<ol>
<li id="fn-bc4a81a2c0-fn-stage">
<p>That is why drawings, sticky notes, zoom, and the PDF all line up with the slide. <a href="#fn-bc4a81a2c0-fnref-stage" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 1" class="data-footnote-backref">↩</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>",
      "id": "sources-go-in-footnotes",
      "index": 19,
      "layout": "default",
      "line": 210,
      "notes": "<p>A footnote. The definition must sit on the same slide as its reference, and it is shown at the bottom of the slide.</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "Sources go in footnotes",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "4d8b862ec3",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h2>A skipped slide</h2></header><div class="s-body"><p>Presenting goes straight past this slide. It stays in the overview, dimmed, for the question you might get.</p></div></div>",
      "id": "a-skipped-slide",
      "index": 20,
      "layout": "default",
      "line": 220,
      "notes": "<p>A skipped slide. The skip directive leaves it out of the talk without deleting it. Press g for the overview and pick it to show it anyway.</p>",
      "options": {
        "skip": true,
      },
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "A skipped slide",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "2a4ad28544",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h2>Fourteen bullets is too many</h2></header><div class="s-body"><ul>
<li>This slide does not fit at full size, so the type steps down until it does</li>
<li>The second bullet adds a qualification that nobody in the room asked for</li>
<li>The third bullet repeats the first one in slightly different words</li>
<li>The fourth bullet introduces an acronym that is never explained again</li>
<li>The fifth bullet is a full sentence that should have been a paragraph</li>
<li>The sixth bullet quotes a statistic without saying where it came from</li>
<li>The seventh bullet is where most of the audience stops reading</li>
<li>The eighth bullet contradicts the second one, but only a little</li>
<li>The ninth bullet lists three examples when one would have done</li>
<li>The tenth bullet was added the night before by someone else</li>
<li>The eleventh bullet refers to a chart that is on a different slide</li>
<li>The twelfth bullet says the same thing as the title of the slide</li>
<li>The thirteenth bullet promises that the next slide will explain everything</li>
<li>The fourteenth bullet is finally the point the slide was trying to make</li>
</ul></div></div>",
      "id": "fourteen-bullets-is-too-many",
      "index": 21,
      "layout": "default",
      "line": 230,
      "notes": "<p>Too much text. When a slide overflows, dex sets its type smaller, in two steps, until it fits. If it still does not fit, the dev server flags it with OVERFLOW.</p>",
      "options": {},
      "steps": 0,
      "title": "Fourteen bullets is too many",
    },
    {
      "attrs": {},
      "hash": "bcd23a56be",
      "html": "<div class="s-main"><header class="s-head"><h1>Your turn</h1></header><div class="s-body"><p>Run <code>pnpm new my-talk</code>, open <code>decks/my-talk/deck.md</code> in your editor, and start writing. Press s for settings and the full list of keys.</p></div></div>",
      "id": "your-turn",
